        <item>
            <title>0.64</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:14:17 +0200</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>202610130911</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.64</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>The bay sits at the end of the south hallway behind one glass door</li>
<li>A crate due a QA carry is carried even when the yard sees the board first</li>
<li>The design docs describe the hall, the vortex and the carries as built</li>
<li>Reconcile drops a guard that could never hold</li>
<li>A repository's untested crates find the column its tested ones took</li>
<li>The pad is the hall's width with five slots in a honeycomb</li>
<li>STATION.md describes the yard that is built</li>
<li>Develop > Restack the Yard</li>
<li>Each repository piles in its own column of the hall</li>
<li>Each scene file draws one thing</li>
<li>Calling off a carry the board took back is the carries' rule</li>
<li>A demo world never reads or writes the saved layout</li>
<li>A rocket's tip stands on its own legs</li>
<li>A tile belongs to one repository</li>
<li>A crate landing in storage launches a ship-on-merge rocket, in one place</li>
<li>Releases and the pad have their own file and their own book</li>
<li>The invariants watchdog goes; what mattered is a model test</li>
<li>A carry carries its own rank</li>
<li>Comments out of the rest of the codebase</li>
<li>Comments out of World, Station, Ledger, Simulation, Jobs, SceneMarkers and Invariants</li>
<li>Where crates stand is the station's, in Yard</li>
<li>The hall is a value of its own</li>
<li>Shuttles and rockets apart; a rocket's tip welds in Rockets</li>
<li>Comments out of the yard's newest files</li>
<li>A carry writes its own landing</li>
<li>Dead code from the pallet, pod and lock era goes</li>
<li>The yard as one hall, its release pulled out by the drones' vortex</li>
<li>STATION.md: the yard as one hall worked by a crane, with testers, one-tile pods, a walkway and no pallet</li>
<li>The payload pod: tested crates wait in their repository's pod on the deck, sealed once all is tested, and go out whole at the merge</li>
<li>Walking, the gate's lock and window and the bay's mouth stand open in the walls</li>
<li>A kick stage flown in under the tip, and an undock in place of a lift-off; the bay's long passage goes</li>
<li>The bay is a hangar under the hull, its mouth held by a field the ships fly through</li>
<li>The cargo lock and the pad's drones: crates cross the hull through a lock, drones work the pad</li>
<li>Air and weight: the hull is the line between minions and drones; the bay is a hangar behind a field, the pad is outside</li>
<li>Wall caps and corner posts stand on the walls again, not piled up in front of the gate robot</li>
<li>The release label clears what the board has no card for, and a cleared card loads the rocket at once</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
